Approach 6 — BFS With Pair, but No vis

This is essentially your approach, and it is important to understand that you don't need a separate visited[][].

Why?

Because this:

grid[nr][nc] = 2;

acts as the visited marker.

Initially:

1 = unvisited fresh
2 = already rotten/visited
0 = empty

When we process:

if (grid[nr][nc] == 1)

we know the cell has not been processed before.

Then immediately:

grid[nr][nc] = 2;

marks it.

Therefore:

Separate visited array ❌
Modify grid directly    ✅

This saves some memory.

