⭐ Most Important Pattern

This problem is another classic:

Multi-Source BFS

The pattern is:

Multiple starting points
        ↓
Put ALL starting points into Queue
        ↓
BFS simultaneously
        ↓
Each BFS level = 1 unit of time
        ↓
First visit = shortest distance/time

For 994 Rotting Oranges:

Source = Rotten oranges (2)
Target = Fresh oranges (1)
Distance = Minutes

For 542 01 Matrix:

Source = Zeros (0)
Target = Ones (1)
Distance = Shortest distance

For 994, remember:

Put every rotten orange into the queue at time 0, then BFS level-by-level. Each level represents one minute.

⭐ Interview-Ready Code

I'd recommend memorizing this version because it is slightly cleaner than storing step in every node:

class Solution {


    public int orangesRotting(int[][] grid) {


        int n = grid.length;
        int m = grid[0].length;


        Queue<int[]> q = new LinkedList<>();


        int fresh = 0;


        // Step 1: Add all rotten oranges
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {


            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {


                if (grid[i][j] == 2) {
                    q.offer(new int[]{i, j});
                } 
                else if (grid[i][j] == 1) {
                    fresh++;
                }
            }
        }


        int time = 0;


        int[] dr = {-1, 0, 1, 0};
        int[] dc = {0, 1, 0, -1};


        // Step 2: Multi-source BFS
        while (!q.isEmpty() && fresh > 0) {


            int size = q.size();


            // One complete level = one minute
            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {


                int[] curr = q.poll();


                int r = curr[0];
                int c = curr[1];


                for (int j = 0; j < 4; j++) {


                    int nr = r + dr[j];
                    int nc = c + dc[j];


                    if (nr >= 0 && nr < n &&
                        nc >= 0 && nc < m &&
                        grid[nr][nc] == 1) {


                        grid[nr][nc] = 2;
                        fresh--;


                        q.offer(new int[]{nr, nc});
                    }
                }
            }


            time++;
        }


        // If fresh oranges remain, they are unreachable
        return fresh == 0 ? time : -1;
    }
}
